                  },
                  {
                    "route": "authoring/ship/checks",
                    "name": "checks",
                    "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
                    "kind": "generic",
                    "title": "Check an integration",
                    "summary": "Pick the check for each problem, learn what fails and what only warns, and run every check in CI.",
                    "sections": [
                      {
                        "id": "pick-a-check",
                        "title": "Pick a check",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Run these in the package folder. The four `doctor integration` checks read your source, and `integration check` runs all four; `integration verify` checks the package npm would publish."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "table",
                            "headers": [
                              "Command",
                              "Proves",
                              "Exits 1 when",
                              "Only warns when"
                            ],
                            "rows": [
                              [
                                "`astryx doctor integration validate`",
                                "The manifest loads, each root holds contributions the CLI can read, and each doc matches its authoring type. Notes list a malformed `cliCommand` (`invalid_cli_command`) and, for each topic, a command written with a package runner (`runner_command`), bare (`plain_command`) or for one package manager (`package_manager_command`), and a token that does not parse (`doc_token`; see `astryx docs authoring/building-blocks/docs/doc-syntax`). Notes fail nothing by default; `integration check --strict --next` fails on the ones marked `next`, and the next minor release counts them",
                                "A declared root is missing (`missing_root`), a contribution does not load (`invalid_doc`, `invalid_component`, `invalid_theme`), or two templates in the package replace one Core id (`ambiguous_template_replacement`)",
                                "The manifest has a key this CLI does not know (`unknown_manifest_key`), or a doc field does not match the doc's authoring type: a field the type does not have, a missing required field, or a value outside the field's type. It also warns on what no reader can serve: a prop listed twice (`duplicate_prop`), a `propDescriptions` key that names no documented prop (`unknown_translated_prop`), a section with no content (`empty_section`), two sections of a topic with one key (`duplicate_section_key`), or a `.doc.zh.mjs` or `.doc.dense.mjs` overlay beside no topic file (`orphan_doc_overlay`). Since 0.7.3 it also lists, from source and without failing, what the package tells apps to import that they cannot: a component's import (the doc's `import`, or the one the CLI derives) or a template's public import whose subpath package.json `exports` does not declare (`component_import_not_exported`, `template_import_not_exported`) or that names another package (`component_import_other_package`); an example that imports an undeclared subpath (`example_import_not_exported`); a template that imports a path outside the templates root (`template_import_outside_root`) or a path its package or Core does not export (`template_private_import`). It lists the same way a component's import whose module does not export the component (`component_import_missing_name`), an example or a template that imports a name its package does not export (`example_import_missing_name`, `template_import_missing_name`), and a template source with no default export (`template_no_default_export`). Each is a note, printed with its fix, that fails `--strict` from the next minor; an import it cannot judge, such as an `exports` target not built yet or a deep path into a `dist/` not built yet, is listed under `publicImports` as not checked. It checks docs with your installed `typescript`, or, where that is missing or has no JavaScript compiler API (TypeScript 7), with an installed `@typescript/typescript6`; without either, it prints `[skip] Docs not type-checked`. With no `astryx.integration.mjs` it prints a hint and exits 0"
                              ],
                              [
                                "`astryx doctor integration components`",
                                "No component name clashes with a Core component, each `replaces` names one Core component, and each component doc's props match the component's TypeScript props",
                                "Core is not installed (`core_not_found`). In a package that declares the CLI range that turns replacement on, a `replaces` target is missing (`missing_component_replacement_target`) or invalid (`invalid_component_replacement`), or two components replace one Core component (`ambiguous_component_replacement`)",
                                "A name clashes with Core, a component sets `replaces` in a package without that range (`inactive_component_replacement`, plus any missing, invalid, or duplicate `replaces` reported as a warning), or a documented prop differs from the code: it is missing there (`not_in_code`), the doc omits a prop the package declares (`not_in_doc`), or its `required` (`required_mismatch`), type (`type_mismatch`), or literal `default` (`default_mismatch`) disagrees, or a `{@link}` in a component doc names no doc (`invalid_doc_graph`). It reads props with your installed `typescript`; without it, it prints `[skip] Props not compared`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "`astryx doctor integration templates`",
                                "Each `replaces` names a Core template of the same type",
                                "A `replaces` target is missing (`missing_template_replacement_target`) or of the other type (`invalid_template_replacement`), or two templates replace one id (`ambiguous_template_replacement`)",
                                "A template id matches a Core id without `replaces`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "`astryx doctor integration docs`",
                                "Your docs tree, every link, topic names against Core, passages two topics repeat word for word, padding phrases and low-density topics, and written pointers to docs",
                                "A topic takes a Core topic name without `replaces` or `extends`, a doc is invalid (`invalid_doc`), or a namespace or placement fails, which hides the doc (`invalid_doc_graph`)",
                                "A link names no doc (`invalid_doc_graph`), two topics repeat a passage word for word (`copied_passage`), prose pads with a listed phrase or falls under the density floor (`doc_fluff`), or prose, a description or summary, or the text of a component doc writes `astryx docs <name>` where a link would be checked (`stray_doc_pointer`)"
                              ],
                              [
                                "`astryx integration check`",
                                "Everything the four `doctor integration` checks prove, in one command, for your build",
                                "Any of the four would exit 1 on its own. With `--strict`, also any warning, and any check that did not run, such as a package with no `astryx.integration.*`",
                                "Anything the four warn about, unless you pass `--strict`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "`astryx integration verify`",
                                "The packed package holds every file, shows the same contributions, resolves every public import, and declares the CLI it needs",
                                "Anything `validate` fails on, no manifest, a file left out of the `.tgz` file, an import that does not resolve, or a missing CLI peer",
                                "Anything `validate` warns about, or a component sets `replaces` and the package does not declare the CLI range that turns it on (`component_replaces_needs_cli`)"
                              ]
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Pass a package name, such as `astryx doctor integration validate @acme/astryx-widgets`, to check an installed copy from an app instead. To fix a props finding, see `astryx docs authoring/building-blocks/components/describe-the-component/check-the-props`."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "run-every-check-in-ci",
                        "title": "Run every check in every build (required)",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Every integration runs `integration check --strict` in its own build, so every build keeps your docs, types, and links in sync; this is required, not optional. The strict check fails on every copied passage the docs check lists (`astryx docs authoring/building-blocks/docs/check-your-docs`). Run `integration verify` before you publish. Install devDependencies first, because the components check needs Core, and `tsc --noEmit` needs `typescript` and a `tsconfig.json`. In package.json:"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "json",
                            "code": "\"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit && astryx integration check --strict\""
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "unordered",
                            "items": [
                              "`integration check` runs `validate`, `components`, `templates`, and `docs` in that order, prints each result, then a summary, and exits 1 when any of them would.",
                              "`--strict` also exits 1 on any warning and on any check that did not run. Without it, warnings keep exit code 0: use that while you fix the warnings a package already has.",
                              "Its exit codes and JSON are a contract for your build: a new check, or a new failure code, joins only in a minor release that names it in the release notes. A patch can still ship a Core component, template, or CLI topic whose name conflicts with one of yours.",
                              "`integration verify` runs `validate` but none of the other three: a Core name clash, a `replaces` that names no Core template, a topic that takes a Core name, or a hidden guide still passes it. Run both before you publish: `astryx integration check --strict && astryx integration verify`.",
                              "Bare `astryx doctor` in the package also warns about a doc section over 32 KB, which no check above measures."
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "what-integration-verify-does",
                        "title": "Verify the packed package",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "`integration verify` packs your package with npm, unpacks it into a temporary app, and checks that the app sees everything your source has. It publishes nothing and leaves no `.tgz` file or temporary folder behind."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "ordered",
                            "items": [
                              "It runs `npm pack` (only with npm: the tarball the registry receives) the way `npm publish` (only with npm: npm is the client the registry publishes from) would, including your `prepack` script.",
                              "It checks that every contribution file is in the `.tgz` file. A root missing from `files` fails with `Add \"templates\" to \"files\" in package.json.`",
                              "It lists the components, templates, themes, docs, and codemods the temporary app sees, and compares them with your source.",
                              "It resolves each component's `import`, and each template's public import, the way Node does, and checks that the module exports the component under the name its doc documents, or a default export for a template. A type-only export does not count.",
                              "For each theme, it rebuilds the source, compares the built module and production CSS with the authored outputs, and proves the module, CSS, and optional font CSS exports resolve from the packed package.",
                              "It fails a package that needs an `@astryxdesign/cli` peer and lacks it: `>=0.6.6` for a template that sets `keywords`, and `>=0.6.4` for a template that sets `replaces`, a docs section, a placed guide, a doc section with an `id`, or a theme."
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "`integration pack --check`, the name this check had before published 0.6.5, still runs it and prints a note; it will be removed in a later release. The options and exit codes are in `astryx docs cli/commands/integration-verify`."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "route": "authoring/ship/versioning",
                    "name": "versioning",
                    "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
                    "kind": "generic",
                    "title": "Versioning",
                    "summary": "Version your package, declare its peers, and keep apps on older CLIs working.",
                    "sections": [
                      {
                        "id": "pick-a-version",
                        "title": "Pick a version",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Version your package with semver: a major version for a breaking change, a minor version for a new feature, and a patch for a fix."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "# 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0: a breaking change\nnpm version major  # only with npm: npm, which every Node install carries, sets the version\n# 1.0.0 -> 1.1.0: a new feature\nnpm version minor  # only with npm: npm, which every Node install carries, sets the version\n# 1.0.0 -> 1.0.1: a fix\nnpm version patch  # only with npm: npm, which every Node install carries, sets the version"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "unordered",
                            "items": [
                              "Before 1.0.0, npm treats each minor version as breaking: an app that asks for `^0.6.0` never gets `0.7.0`. Bump the minor version for a breaking change, and the patch for anything else.",
                              "Ship a codemod with each breaking change so apps can migrate; see `astryx docs authoring/building-blocks/codemods`."
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "know-what-breaks-apps",
                        "title": "Know what breaks apps",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "A breaking change stops code, commands, or links that worked in an app from working after the upgrade. For an integration, these names are part of its API."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "table",
                            "headers": [
                              "You change or remove",
                              "What stops working in the app"
                            ],
                            "rows": [
                              [
                                "A component name, such as `AcmeCarousel`",
                                "Imports, and `astryx component AcmeCarousel`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "A template id, such as `acme-dashboard`",
                                "`astryx template acme-dashboard`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "A theme slug, such as `ocean`",
                                "`astryx theme add ocean`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "A topic name or route, such as `acme/deploying`",
                                "Reads of the old name, and links to it from other docs"
                              ],
                              [
                                "A component's `import` path",
                                "Imports written from the old path"
                              ],
                              [
                                "An `exports` entry",
                                "Imports of that path, which fail with `ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "A prop",
                                "Code that passes it"
                              ]
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "List each breaking change in your release notes, with the codemod that migrates it. Any changelog tool works. If `package.json` has a `files` allowlist, add `CHANGELOG.md` to it so npm packs it."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "declare-peer-ranges",
                        "title": "Declare peer ranges",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Declare the Astryx packages that your code imports as peer dependencies, in `peerDependencies`, so the app installs one copy of each. Keep each range as wide as your tests prove."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "table",
                            "headers": [
                              "Peer",
                              "Declare it when",
                              "Range"
                            ],
                            "rows": [
                              [
                                "`@astryxdesign/core`",
                                "Your code imports Core, as a theme does with `@astryxdesign/core/theme`",
                                "The Core versions you test, such as `^0.6.0`"
                              ],
                              [
                                "`@astryxdesign/theme-*`",
                                "Your code imports that theme package",
                                "The versions you test"
                              ],
                              [
                                "`@astryxdesign/cli`",
                                "You ship a docs section, a placed guide, a template that sets `replaces` or `keywords`, a component that sets `replaces`, a doc section with an `id`, or a theme",
                                "`>=0.6.6` when you ship a template that sets `keywords`, `>=0.6.7` when a component sets `replaces`, otherwise `>=0.6.4`. Optional in `peerDependenciesMeta`"
                              ]
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "json",
                            "code": "{\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@astryxdesign/core\": \"^0.6.0\",\n    \"@astryxdesign/cli\": \">=0.6.4\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependenciesMeta\": {\n    \"@astryxdesign/cli\": {\"optional\": true}\n  }\n}"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "`integration verify` fails a package that needs the CLI peer and lacks it, or whose range admits a stable CLI too old for what it ships. `integration add doc --parent` and `integration add theme` write the peer for you."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "When the CLI is outside that range, `doctor integration validate` and `integration check` list a `cli_peer_version` note naming your package. A note fails nothing, `--strict` included, and `integration verify` does not report it. Below the range the note gives the commands that install a newer Core and CLI together, as dev dependencies in your own package folder, and then run `upgrade --apply`. Above it, in an app the note asks for a release of your package that supports that CLI, and in your own package folder it asks you to test your package with that CLI and widen the range."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "support-older-clis",
                        "title": "Support older CLIs",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "An app may run an older CLI than the one you build with. A CLI reads what it knows and skips the rest, but some newer files make an older CLI hide your docs."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "unordered",
                            "items": [
                              "An unknown field in `astryx.integration.mjs` is ignored with an `unknown_manifest_key` warning, and the rest of the manifest still loads.",
                              "A named export that the CLI does not know is ignored with no warning, so `debug` and `gapReport` are safe to add.",
                              "Published 0.6.3 and earlier print each `{@link ...}` as written.",
                              "Published 0.6.3 and earlier reject a template that sets `replaces` or `keywords`, drop that template, and hide every doc topic your package ships. Published 0.6.4 and 0.6.5 still drop a template that sets `keywords`.",
                              "Published 0.6.3 and earlier cannot read a docs section, a section `id`, or a theme folder that `integration add theme` writes. They can then hide every doc topic your package ships.",
                              "Published 0.6.2 and 0.6.3 still load your components, but published 0.6.0 and 0.6.1 cannot read the component docs that `integration add component` writes: `component AcmeCarousel` fails there.",
                              "An app on an older CLI lists a component whose doc names another export of its file under the file name, and lists no family members, so `component AcmeCarousel` fails there."
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "`integration verify` requires the CLI peer for a docs section, a placed guide, a template `replaces` or `keywords`, a doc section with an `id`, and a theme. A CLI too old for one of them cannot read it, and when it hides your topics, `docs` gives no warning."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "codemods-and-versions",
                        "title": "Name codemod folders after Core versions",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Name each codemod folder after the Core version whose upgrade should run it, not after your package's version. Which folders an app runs, and when, is in \"Choose when a codemod runs\" in `astryx docs authoring/building-blocks/codemods`."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "route": "authoring/ship/publishing",
                    "name": "publishing",
                    "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
                    "kind": "generic",
                    "title": "Publish an integration",
                    "summary": "Publish your package to npm under the right release tag, checking it before and after.",
                    "sections": [
                      {
                        "id": "check-before-you-publish",
                        "title": "Check before you publish",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Publish only a package that passes every check, then preview the upload with `npm publish --dry-run` (only with npm: publishing goes through npm, which every Node install carries). The dry run lists the files and the tag without uploading."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "astryx doctor integration validate && astryx doctor integration components && astryx doctor integration templates && astryx doctor integration docs && astryx integration verify\nnpm publish --dry-run --access public  # only with npm: publishing goes through npm, which every Node install carries"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "text",
                            "code": "npm notice Publishing to https://registry.npmjs.org/ with tag latest and public access (dry-run)\n+ @acme/astryx-widgets@1.0.0"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Set a new `version` for each release; `astryx docs authoring/ship/versioning` covers what counts as breaking. What each check proves is in `astryx docs authoring/ship/checks`."
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "keep-private-files-out",
                        "title": "Keep private files out",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "With no `files` list, npm packs every file your ignore files do not exclude, including an old `.tgz` file or an `.env` file. List what ships instead."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "npm pkg set 'files[]=components' 'files[]=templates' 'files[]=themes' 'files[]=docs' 'files[]=codemods' 'files[]=astryx.integration.mjs'  # only with npm: edits package.json\nnpm pack --dry-run  # only with npm: builds the tarball npm publishes"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "unordered",
                            "items": [
                              "List only the roots you ship, and always `astryx.integration.mjs`. npm adds package.json, and a README and LICENSE when you have them.",
                              "Each later `integration add` appends its root to the list.",
                              "`integration verify` fails when a root is missing from the list, and names the root to add to `files` (the message is in `astryx docs authoring/help/troubleshooting`)."
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "publish-to-npm",
                        "title": "Publish to npm",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "A scoped package is private by default, so publish it with `--access public`. Without `--tag`, npm tags the release `latest`, which is what `npm install @acme/astryx-widgets` installs."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "# Publish a release\nnpm publish --access public  # only with npm: publishing goes through npm, which every Node install carries\n\n# Or set the access once in package.json\nnpm pkg set publishConfig.access=public  # only with npm: Yarn has no pkg command"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "To let apps try a release first, publish it under `next`, then point `latest` at it once ready."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "# Only apps that ask for next get it: npm install @acme/astryx-widgets@next\nnpm publish --tag next  # only with npm: publishing goes through npm, which every Node install carries\n\n# Make that version the default\nnpm dist-tag add @acme/astryx-widgets@1.1.0 latest  # only with npm: dist-tags are set with npm, which every Node install carries\nnpm dist-tag ls @acme/astryx-widgets  # only with npm: dist-tags are set with npm, which every Node install carries"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "check-the-published-package",
                        "title": "Check the published package",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Install the version you published in a clean app, and run the same commands you ran against the `.tgz` file."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "mkdir check-release && cd check-release\nnpm init -y  # only with npm: npm, which every Node install carries, writes the package.json\nnpm install @astryxdesign/core @astryxdesign/cli @acme/astryx-widgets@1.0.0\nastryx component AcmeCarousel\nastryx doctor integration validate @acme/astryx-widgets"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "The full list of commands to run in an app is in `astryx docs authoring/ship/test-in-an-app`. To help apps move to the new version, see `astryx docs authoring/ship/upgrading`."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "route": "authoring/ship/upgrading",
                    "name": "upgrading",
                    "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
                    "kind": "generic",
                    "title": "Upgrading",
                    "summary": "Update your package for each Astryx release, and help apps upgrade with it.",
                    "sections": [
                      {
                        "id": "update-for-a-new-astryx-release",
                        "title": "Update for a new Astryx release",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "When Astryx ships a release, bump your devDependencies, rerun the checks, widen your peer ranges, and ship a codemod for each change that breaks apps."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "# 1. Build and test against the new release\nnpm install -D @astryxdesign/cli@latest @astryxdesign/core@latest\n# 2. Rerun the checks\nastryx doctor integration validate\nastryx doctor integration docs\nastryx integration verify\n# 3. Admit the new Core once the checks pass\nnpm pkg set 'peerDependencies.@astryxdesign/core=^0.6.0 || ^0.7.0'  # only with npm: edits package.json\n# 4. Migrate apps across a change that breaks them\nastryx integration add codemod rename-delay --to 0.7.0"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "unordered",
                            "items": [
                              "Run every check in `astryx docs authoring/ship/checks`, not only the ones shown.",
                              "Codemod folders are named for Core versions: `astryx docs authoring/building-blocks/codemods`.",
                              "Release the result as a new version of your package; see `astryx docs authoring/ship/publishing`."
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "upgrade-an-app",
                        "title": "Upgrade an app",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "After an app installs a new Core, `astryx upgrade` runs the codemods for the versions it crossed. It is a dry run by default; `--apply` writes the changes."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "bash",
                            "code": "# Preview what would change; nothing is written\nastryx upgrade --from 0.6.3 --integration @acme/astryx-widgets\n# Write the changes\nastryx upgrade --from 0.6.3 --integration @acme/astryx-widgets --apply"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "text",
                            "code": "Integrations: @acme/astryx-widgets\n<n> codemods to run\nApplying integration codemods...\n  Rename AcmeCarousel delay to interval (v0.7.0, @acme/astryx-widgets)\n[ok]     [ok] src/Hero.tsx"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "unordered",
                            "items": [
                              "`--from` is the `@astryxdesign/core` version the app had before, and the target is the installed Core.",
                              "`--integration` names your package. Without it, or an `integrations` entry in `astryx.config`, the upgrade skips your codemods, even when the app has your package installed.",
                              "`<n>` includes Core's codemods for the same versions, which run first.",
                              "Put this command in your release notes."
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "know-which-files-upgrades-skip",
                        "title": "Know which files upgrades skip",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "Upgrades never write files that the app marks as generated, vendored, or ignored. When such a file still needs a codemod change, the upgrade stops with `ERR_CODEMOD_PROTECTED` and exit code 1."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "list",
                            "style": "unordered",
                            "items": [
                              "Generated: an `@generated` comment at the top of the file, or `linguist-generated` in `.gitattributes`.",
                              "Vendored: `linguist-vendored` in `.gitattributes`.",
                              "Ignored: a match in `.gitignore` or `.hgignore`."
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "code",
                            "lang": "text",
                            "code": "!     ! src/gen/Gen.tsx - protected by @generated in the leading comment block\nERR_CODEMOD_PROTECTED: 1 protected file still requires a codemod change:\n  src/gen/Gen.tsx — @generated in the leading comment block\nUpgrade incomplete: protected changes remain"
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "The upgrade still writes every other file. Its options and exit codes are in `astryx docs cli/commands/upgrade`."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "route": "authoring/help",
            "name": "help",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "namespace",
            "title": "Help",
            "summary": "Find a CLI message and how to fix it.",
            "content": [],
            "slots": [
              {
                "name": "guides",
                "title": "Help",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "route": "authoring/help/troubleshooting",
                    "name": "troubleshooting",
                    "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
                    "kind": "generic",
                    "title": "Troubleshooting",
                    "summary": "Find the message the CLI printed while you build, verify, or install an integration, and apply its fix.",
                    "sections": [
                      {
                        "id": "fix-setup-errors",
                        "title": "Fix setup errors",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "These appear while you start the package or run the CLI in it. Each row quotes what the CLI prints."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "table",
                            "headers": [
                              "Message",
                              "Fix"
                            ],
                            "rows": [
                              [
                                "`No package.json found. Run this command inside an integration package.`",
                                "Run `npm init -y` (only with npm: writes package.json) and `npm pkg set name=@acme/astryx-widgets` (only with npm: edits package.json) first, in the package folder."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`Error: Could not find @astryxdesign/core package`",
                                "Component commands read Core. Run `npm install -D @astryxdesign/core` in the package."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`core_not_found`: `Could not resolve @astryxdesign/core, so component names could not be checked.`",
                                "Same fix. The check exits 1."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`Error: unknown subcommand 'integration verify'`, or `Error: Pass --check to verify the integration tarball.`",
                                "Your CLI is older than `integration verify`. Run `npm install -D @astryxdesign/cli@latest`. On the older CLI, the same check is `integration pack --check`."
                              ],
                              [
                                "Note: `integration pack --check` is deprecated.",
                                "The old name still runs the same check. Switch to `astryx integration verify`; the old name will be removed in a later release."
                              ]
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "id": "fix-verify-failures",
                        "title": "Fix integration verify failures",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "prose",
                            "text": "`astryx integration verify` prints each failure as a `[fail]` line. Add `--json` to see its issue code, such as `component_export_missing`."
                          },
                          {
                            "type": "table",
                            "headers": [
                              "Message",
                              "Fix"
                            ],
                            "rows": [
                              [
                                "`component_export_missing`: `Component \"AcmeCarousel\" advertises import \"@acme/astryx-widgets/components/AcmeCarousel\", but that packed module does not export \"AcmeCarousel\".`",
                                "package.json has no `exports` map, or the module does not export the name. Keep `export function AcmeCarousel`, and add the entry: `npm pkg set 'exports[./components/AcmeCarousel]=./components/AcmeCarousel.tsx'` (only with npm: edits package.json). When the quoted name is a file name, such as `acme-carousel`, set the doc's `name` to the component the file exports. A type-only export does not count."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`template_export_missing`: `Template \"acme-dashboard\" public import \"@acme/astryx-widgets/templates/acme-dashboard\" does not have a default export.`",
                                "Run `npm pkg set 'exports[./templates/acme-dashboard]=./templates/acme-dashboard.tsx'` (only with npm: edits package.json), and keep `export default` in the source. Start new packages with `\"exports\": {}` so each add writes these."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`component_import_unresolvable` or `template_import_unresolvable`: `…Package subpath './components/AcmeCarousel' is not defined by \"exports\"…`",
                                "The `exports` map has no entry for it. Run `npm pkg set 'exports[./components/AcmeCarousel]=./components/AcmeCarousel.tsx'` (only with npm: edits package.json), or `'exports[./templates/acme-dashboard]=./templates/acme-dashboard.tsx'` for a template."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`component_import_unresolvable`: `…but a consumer cannot resolve it: Cannot find package '@acme/old-name'`",
                                "You renamed the package after the add wrote each doc's `import`. Change `import` in every component doc to the new name."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`Declared templates root \"templates\" has 0 of 2 expected files in the pack list. Add \"templates\" to \"files\" in package.json.`",
                                "Run `npm pkg set 'files[]=templates'` (only with npm: edits package.json)."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`docs_tree_needs_cli`: `The package ships a namespace doc or a placed guide but declares no @astryxdesign/cli peer.`",
                                "Run `npm pkg set 'peerDependencies.@astryxdesign/cli=>=0.6.4'` (only with npm: edits package.json) and `npm pkg set 'peerDependenciesMeta.@astryxdesign/cli.optional=true' --json` (only with npm: edits package.json)."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`replaces_needs_cli`: The package has a template that sets `replaces` but declares no @astryxdesign/cli peer.",
                                "Run `npm pkg set 'peerDependencies.@astryxdesign/cli=>=0.6.4'` (only with npm: edits package.json) and `npm pkg set 'peerDependenciesMeta.@astryxdesign/cli.optional=true' --json` (only with npm: edits package.json). A stable CLI before 0.6.4 rejects `replaces`, drops that template, and hides your doc topics."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`component_replaces_needs_cli` (a warning): The package has a component that sets `replaces` but declares no @astryxdesign/cli peer, or a peer range that admits an earlier CLI.",
                                "Run `npm pkg set 'peerDependencies.@astryxdesign/cli=>=0.6.7'` (only with npm: edits package.json) and `npm pkg set 'peerDependenciesMeta.@astryxdesign/cli.optional=true' --json` (only with npm: edits package.json) to turn the replacement on. Until then apps see no change (`astryx docs authoring/building-blocks/components/replace-a-core-component`)."
                              ],
                              [
                                "`keywords_needs_cli`: The package has a template that sets `keywords` but declares no @astryxdesign/cli peer.",
