              },
              {
                "id": "discover-source",
                "title": "DiscoverSource",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "prose",
                    "text": "A source for `astryx discover`: an async function that returns a catalog of packages a project could add, their versions, and what each version adds. Set it as `discover` in astryx.config, or export it as `discover` from an integration manifest. Discover calls every source, the project one first, and then reads the official list the CLI carries; another source's entry for an official package is kept. A source that throws, runs past 30 seconds, or returns an invalid catalog never hides the others; discover then uses the last good answer that source gave for the same request, or reports the source as failed when it saved none. Discover only reads: it prints the command that adds a package and never runs it."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "prose",
                    "text": "Applies to: `discover` in astryx.config.*, or the `discover` named export of astryx.integration.*"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "table",
                    "headers": [
                      "Field",
                      "Type",
                      "Required",
                      "Description"
                    ],
                    "rows": [
                      [
                        "context",
                        "DiscoverSourceContext",
                        "yes",
                        "The one argument the source is called with."
                      ],
                      [
                        "context.signal",
                        "AbortSignal",
                        "yes",
                        "Aborted when the source runs past 30 seconds."
                      ],
                      [
                        "context.package",
                        "string",
                        "no",
                        "Set when discover shows one package: return that package with every version."
                      ],
                      [
                        "context.version",
                        "string",
                        "no",
                        "With `package`: return that version's contributions. Without it, the latest release's."
                      ],
                      [
                        "returns",
                        "Promise<DiscoverCatalog>",
                        "yes",
                        "The catalog. Discover checks it, ignores fields and item kinds it does not know, and refuses any schemaVersion but 1."
                      ],
                      [
                        "schemaVersion",
                        "1",
                        "yes",
                        "Version of the catalog shape."
                      ],
                      [
                        "source",
                        "{name: string, generatedAt: string, complete: boolean}",
                        "yes",
                        "Who answered, when the data was produced (ISO 8601), and false when the source knows its list is partial."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages",
                        "DiscoverPackage[]",
                        "yes",
                        "One entry per npm package. When two sources list the same package, the earlier source wins."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages[].package",
                        "string",
                        "yes",
                        "The npm name."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages[].integration",
                        "string",
                        "yes",
                        "Shared by every npm name that publishes the same integration. Discover lists an integration once."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages[].aliases",
                        "string[]",
                        "yes",
                        "The integration's other npm names. Discover never offers a package the project has under another name."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages[].description",
                        "string",
                        "no",
                        "One line, for the list and search."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages[].latest",
                        "string | null",
                        "yes",
                        "The latest release. Null when there are only prereleases."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages[].versions",
                        "DiscoverVersion[]",
                        "yes",
                        "Every version, newest first: `{version, publishedAt, prerelease, status}`, where status is `ok` or why the version could not be read."
                      ],
                      [
                        "packages[].contributions",
                        "DiscoverContribution[]",
                        "yes",
                        "What the requested (else latest) version adds: `{kind, name, title?, summary?, keywords?}`, where kind is `component`, `template`, `doc`, `theme`, `codemod`, or `agent-doc` (a DiscoverKind) and name is the name the CLI uses for it."
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "code",
                    "lang": "js",
                    "code": "export default {\n  async discover({signal, package: name, version}) {\n    const res = await fetch(catalogUrl(name, version), {signal});\n    return res.json();\n  },\n};",
                    "label": "A project source in astryx.config"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "prose",
                    "text": "In global mode: the discover source of an integration installed for the computer is called in folders outside any project; inside a project, only the sources of integrations the project installs are. See `astryx docs global` and `astryx docs authoring/global-integrations`."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "codemod",
                "title": "Astryx Codemod",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "prose",
                    "text": "A codemod module the CLI runs during `astryx upgrade`. Default-export a plain object with a `type` discriminant: 'code' rewrites source files, 'config' rewrites the astryx.config.* file. There is no factory to call."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "prose",
                    "text": "Applies to: `<codemods>/<version>/<id>.{ts,mjs,js}` in an integration package: `<codemods>` is the codemods root of astryx.integration.*, and `<version>` is the exact @astryxdesign/core version (such as 0.7.0) whose upgrade runs the codemod. A file directly in the root never runs."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "table",
                    "headers": [
                      "Field",
                      "Type",
                      "Required",
                      "Description"
                    ],
                    "rows": [
                      [
                        "title",
                        "string",
                        "yes",
                        "Short, human-readable title shown in upgrade output. Example: 'Rename Button prop kind to variant'."
