        "type": "prose",
        "text": "In global mode: users can install your integration for their computer, beside the global CLI. It then applies in folders outside any project, and inside a project only if the project installs it. See `astryx docs global` and `astryx docs authoring/global-integrations`."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "An integration is a way to share things with Astryx users: a package you own and maintain, built on a framework Astryx gives you. Publish one, many, or any mix, and people install it in one step. It works with the Astryx CLI alongside Core. See each kind under `astryx docs authoring/building-blocks`."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "For example, ship a carousel as an integration. Any app that installs it can find it with `astryx search carousel`, and the CLI uses it like any Astryx Core component."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "An integration can also replace a built-in template or doc. To start, install `@astryxdesign/cli` and open `astryx docs authoring/quick-start`."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Every field of every file you write for an integration is in `astryx docs authoring/field-reference`."
      },
